    "scientific_conclusion": "The steep-scarp joint inversion is model-dependent. Under the conservative raw spatial noise model, zero motion is contained in the 95% confidence interval (Ensemble: [-651, +106] mm/yr; CTRL-01: [-626, +131] mm/yr). Under the ramp-removed (detrended) null model, an apparent signal appears at ~3.7-sigma (Ensemble: -390 +/- 105 mm/yr; CTRL-01: -327 +/- 105 mm/yr). This apparent signal is directed upslope (v < 0), which is physically implausible as gravitational slope creep and is consistent with residual atmospheric phase delays or reference-pixel drift across steep alpine relief, but two pilot pairs cannot resolve this. Single pilot pairs cannot detect slope creep below roughly 0.2 to 0.5 m/yr, and the two pilot pairs constrain slope-parallel creep only to within a few tenths of a metre per year."
